+### [Renoised Score Distillation (RSD)](16424-renoised-score-distillation-rsd.md)
+Renoised Score Distillation (RSD) is a score-distillation objective designed for 2D image super-resolution that combines the structural consistency of Score Distillation Sampling (SDS) with the detail generation of ancestral sampling. It solves the problem of generating high-resolution images that are both sharp and consistent with low-resolution conditioning by optimizing intermediate denoised latents along a linearly decreasing time schedule. Unlike standard SDS which operates in $z_0$ space, RSD formulates a loss function to backpropagate gradients through the intermediate latent $z'_{t-1}$, allowing it to produce sharper details than SDS while maintaining better low-resolution consistency than pure ancestral sampling. See [Renoised Score Distillation (RSD)](16424-renoised-score-distillation-rsd.md).
 
